00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:41.461
And this is related to memory tuning,
which turns

166
00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:44.831
any LLM into a million way
mixture of expert adapters.

167
00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:48.100
And those adapters are using path
to using parameter efficient fine-tuning.

168
00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:51.270
And that reduces, the time by 240 times.

169
00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.941
So there are many ways to dramatically
reduce, the time for fine-tuning.

170
00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:58.177
And I think the future might look
a little bit interesting with fine-tuning

171
00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:01.180
being, similar
to the time of building a RAG index.

172
00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:05.117
But to get these efficiency gains, it's
actually fairly difficult.

173
00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:08.154
So you have to implement
